    {
      "title": "Indigo signs $328 mn finance deal with Citi to buy for 8 Airbus aircraft",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/aviation/indigo-signs-328-mn-finance-deal-with-citi-to-buy-for-8-airbus-aircraft-126101300655_1.html",
      "description": "Country's largest carrier Indigo has signed a USD 328 million financing deal with Citi to buy eight narrow-body planes to be manufactured by Airbus.\nThis is the world's first aviation financing transaction insured by the Belgian export credit agency (ECA) Credendo, and the maiden ECA-backed aircraft financing structured through the GIFT IFSC, according to a statement.\nThe financing will help Indigo procure six A321s and two A320s, it said.\nGlobal banking major Citi acted as sole mandated arranger, ECA coordinator and sole lender, with the financing backed by Credendo's credit insurance, it added.\nThe transaction was executed through Indigo's subsidiary, InterGlobe Aviation Financial Services IFSC and provides a \"competitive and diversified source of long-term funding\" for the carrier's fleet and network growth, it said.\n\"By combining Citi's cross-border aviation and ECA financing expertise with Credendo's credit insurance and IndiGo's GIFT IFSC platform, we have delivered a ...",
